{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq '.result' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/game_technical_director.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"alternative_architecture\": {\n    \"description\": \"Replace the milestone stack with a thin delivery-first loop. State: keep the GDD, Git main, and small versioned contracts only for active/near-term slices; derive operational status from persisted run state, Git/PR state, and validation manifests. Planning: a human selects the next vertical slice and approves its behavior; an LLM produces a bounded contract plus GDD-section impact map. Execution: a local driver creates one branch/worktree and invokes one write-capable worker, followed by a fresh reviewer. Validation: run deterministic checks and Unity compile/EditMode/PlayMode tests through the clean runner, then require human checks for feel and visuals. Recovery: persist a small state machine—planned, implementing, validating, needs-repair, needs-human, merged—with commits, evidence paths, and bounded retry counts. GDD changes: map changed sections or stable requirement IDs only to affected contracts, classifying them as unaffected, contract-review, revalidation, or rework; never globally rebuild the backlog by default. Unity integration: the Windows Unity host owns engine execution, outputs XML/logs outside the repository, checks tree cleanliness, and distinguishes in-memory builders from committed scene/prefab conformance.\",\n    \"needed\": true,\n    \"why_better\": \"It retains the safety mechanisms supported by actual failures while making gameplay delivery the primary proof. It eliminates several authority handoffs, handles an iterative GDD causally instead of through a whole-document hash, and can produce useful game progress before scheduling, artifact generation, or parallelism exist.\"\n  },\n  \"architecture_summary\": \"The repository contains four substantial production foundations: a 37-contract TaskGraph, validated GDD retrieval, evidence-derived conformance, and provider-neutral read/review invocation. It does not contain the production path that creates throughput: no enabled readiness, dispatch authorization, write-capable gameplay worker, execution crew, Git lifecycle, Unity execution, merge loop, or completion propagation. The result is a sophisticated safety and audit shell around a small Unity prototype, not yet an autonomous game-development system.\",\n  \"biggest_uncertainty\": \"The frozen repository cannot show whether a separate development machine can execute reliable automated Unity runs for new work. It records credible prior Unity 6000.1.8f1 results, but no new production task has traversed the proposed end-to-end loop.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"do_not_build_yet\": [\n    \"Continuous scheduling and backlog replenishment\",\n    \"Parallel workers, generalized leases, and resource-lock scheduling\",\n    \"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization\",\n    \"Automatic merge or provider fallback\",\n    \"The bundled Progressive Decomposer platform\",\n    \"Artifact Authority and Artifact GER until a real design artifact blocks delivery\",\n    \"More provider adapters or ArchitectureReview plumbing\",\n    \"Top-k-only context packs presented as complete canon\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Successful read-only diagnostics at the frozen commit reported 37 valid schema-v2 contracts, an acyclic graph, disabled autonomous dispatch, unavailable readiness, zero authorized tasks, and a clean working tree before and after.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"NSC-023 derives as conformant from its committed baseline, demonstrating that the evidence evaluator works for one historical feature.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The production GDD index validated as CURRENT with 41 chunks and matching source hash, but documentation says the whole GDD must still be supplied because retrieval coverage is unproven.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/GDDRAG\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"AgentRuntime explicitly lacks repository writing, approved command execution, gameplay roles, Unity, GER, task selection, Git workflow, readiness, and authorization.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"TaskExecution is currently only an immutable task-identity wrapper around one generic invocation.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskExecution/task_runner.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"NSC-003 declares itself concrete and single-agent, while current-state guidance identifies unresolved input arbitration, steering, cancellation, arrival, pathing, and restriction semantics.\",\n      \"path\": \"Tasks/NSC-003.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The GDD still names Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity as canonical, while implementation and evidence moved authority to Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\",\n      \"path\": \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The conformance evaluator compares every evidence record against the hash of the entire current GDD, so any GDD text change makes otherwise unchanged evidence stale.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The camera GER passed static review twice while remaining unusable in Unity, then encountered a no-op refinement before succeeding through runtime feedback and bounded retries.\",\n      \"path\": \"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Earlier builder tests called the production scene-saving entry point; later commits added an in-memory seam, direct committed-scene tests, and byte-preservation checks.\",\n      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The actual project still has direct hardware polling for WASD and door interaction, no spells or enemy runtime, missing required navigation packages, and no registered build scene.\",\n      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Across the 244 commits after the camera feature commit, 136 touched Pipeline, only three touched Assets/NoSafeCircle, and none touched runtime gameplay scripts; those three game-area changes were scene/test safety work rather than a new mechanic.\",\n      \"path\": \"Git history: 20c5228..9f2485d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Pipeline areas contain roughly 13,000 nonblank lines across TaskGraph, GDDRAG, AgentRuntime, and TaskExecution, versus roughly 1,448 under Assets/NoSafeCircle; Reconciliation adds about 84,000 nonblank lines including generated history.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"CURRENT_STATE contains contradictory lifecycle claims: its opening describes Stage 4C/Codex migration as implemented, while its later Immediate Next Goal says Claude migration is next and Codex remains unimplemented.\",\n      \"path\": \"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gdd_iteration_concerns\": [\n    \"The present whole-GDD hash treats an unrelated wording, art, balance, or repository-description edit as grounds to revalidate every delivered task.\",\n    \"Contracts copy substantial GDD prose and bootstrap repository observations, creating a second version of design/current-state facts that can drift independently.\",\n    \"Stable requirement IDs and an implemented requirement-to-task impact map do not exist.\",\n    \"The promised reconciliation-to-graph diff/review/apply path is not implemented, so immutable snapshots do not synchronize the living graph.\",\n    \"The scene relocation demonstrates the problem now: canon, contract bootstrap evidence, current implementation, and conformance evidence disagree on the canonical path while NSC-023 still derives as conformant.\",\n    \"When canon changes, the correct flow should be scoped impact review: identify affected requirements, amend or supersede only affected contracts, decide revalidation versus rework, preserve prior delivery evidence as lineage, and deterministically recalculate affected dependencies.\",\n    \"Full reconciliation should be reserved for major scope changes, milestone audits, or evidence that the graph has materially diverged—not normal iterative GDD editing.\"\n  ],\n  \"human_intervention_points\": [\n    \"Approve gameplay semantics where the GDD leaves feel, arbitration, cancellation, navigation, or tuning ambiguous.\",\n    \"Play the game to judge movement feel, camera framing, readability, animation, encounter pacing, balance, and fun.\",\n    \"Inspect scene, prefab, package, Input Actions, and build-configuration changes before merge.\",\n    \"Resolve architectural changes and cross-system ownership conflicts discovered during implementation.\",\n    \"Approve canon amendments, contract supersession, and generated design/content.\",\n    \"Review and merge changes until the single-ticket lane has a strong production track record.\",\n    \"Perform final Windows build, device/input, performance, and presentation validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"hypothetical_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"Parallel resource locks and generalized claims protect against multi-worker conflicts before one production worker exists.\",\n    \"GitHub dashboard synchronization addresses visibility at a scale the project has not reached.\",\n    \"Automatic provider fallback protects availability but risks changing behavior and is not an observed delivery blocker.\",\n    \"Artifact Authority, artifact promotion, and multi-evaluator Artifact GER address future generated-design work; the current bootstrap contains zero artifact tasks.\",\n    \"Continuous scheduling, backlog replenishment, merge queues, and daily budget governance protect later unattended scale.\",\n    \"Most adversarial immutable-evidence ancestry and ambiguity cases are prudent hardening but have not materially accelerated the one existing production baseline.\",\n    \"Top-k context optimization addresses future token cost, while the current policy still sends the entire relatively small GDD.\"\n  ],\n  \"missing_components\": [\n    \"An approved dependency-readiness rule derived from current conformance\",\n    \"A write-capable, scope-bounded implementation invocation\",\n    \"A minimal branch/worktree execution driver\",\n    \"Task-specific Unity compile, EditMode, PlayMode, and committed-artifact validation\",\n    \"A small persisted recovery state machine around one delivery attempt\",\n    \"A deterministic diff between evolving canon, task contracts, and delivered surfaces\",\n    \"A reviewed mechanism for amending or superseding affected contracts\",\n    \"A proven context builder that cannot omit cross-cutting canon\",\n    \"Actual gameplay integration through review, merge, evidence publication, and downstream readiness\"\n  ],\n  \"next_slice\": {\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"A short human-approved decision note resolving primary click, held-pointer steering, UI click suppression, command replacement/cancellation, arrival behavior, and prototype pathing expectations\",\n      \"Input Actions-backed pointer position and primary-click actions\",\n      \"PlayerMovement-owned world-space pointer projection and destination/hold steering\",\n      \"Owner-controlled movement restriction, suspend/re-enable, and restart interfaces\",\n      \"Integration with door selection so one click can request approach without independent pointer projection\",\n      \"Focused component and Play Mode tests using non-saving seams\",\n      \"A clean-tree Unity validation run with external XML/logs\",\n      \"Human Play Mode approval for movement feel, camera framing, UI arbitration, and door approach\",\n      \"One reviewed merge plus minimal delivery manifest sufficient to derive task conformance and unlock dependencies\"\n    ],\n    \"proof_of_value\": \"Starting from one approved contract, a bounded worker creates a gameplay diff, survives deterministic and Unity validation, incorporates runtime feedback through at most a small fixed repair budget, receives human feel approval, merges, and causes dependent work to become ready. That is the first credible demonstration of days-versus-weeks leverage.\",\n    \"title\": \"Playable mouse movement and door-approach delivery lane\",\n    \"why\": \"Movement is foundational to spells, doors, pursuit, restart, and victory suspension. It also exercises every currently unproven production boundary: design clarification, Input Actions, write execution, canonical-scene integration, runtime validation, repair, merge, conformance, and dependency propagation. Build only the narrow glue needed for this slice.\"\n  },\n  \"observed_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"Repository-backed state prevents loss of context between model sessions.\",\n    \"Bounded contracts reduced scope drift in the door, mana, and camera coursework runs.\",\n    \"Runtime evidence re-entering GER fixed camera defects that semantic/static review approved incorrectly.\",\n    \"No-op change detection prevented a refiner from claiming progress without modifying gameplay files.\",\n    \"Circuit breakers bounded repeated camera repair.\",\n    \"The Unity testing policy, clean runner, in-memory builder seam, and committed-scene checks directly address tests that previously saved canonical assets.\",\n    \"Scene identity/location checks address duplicate or ambiguous DoorPrototype scene authority.\",\n    \"Immutable reconciliation outputs and resume utilities address real reconciliation timeout, recovery, identity, and merge-conflict problems—although those are pipeline-self-management wins rather than game throughput.\",\n    \"Current production GDDRAG addresses the observed staleness of the older July Assignment 4 index.\",\n    \"Line-ending normalization addresses the repository's Windows/Linux validation boundary.\"\n  ],\n  \"overall_verdict\": \"partially_unsound\",\n  \"overengineering\": [\n    \"A multi-model, domain-parallel reconciliation and verification system was built before one production gameplay ticket could execute.\",\n    \"The one-time 37-contract bootstrap required extensive schema, refinement, recovery, finding-identity, and arbitration machinery disproportionate to this small game.\",\n    \"TaskGraph completion was replaced by a task-specific immutable evidence/conformance system before replacement readiness shipped, leaving the graph inert.\",\n    \"AgentRuntime has extensive hostile-value, schema, path, transport, and publication hardening while its providers remain incapable of implementing gameplay.\",\n    \"ArchitectureReview was chosen as the first production runtime consumer, proving review transport rather than game delivery.\",\n    \"Task contract, evidence record, conformance result, readiness, authorization, runtime request, task-execution request, reconciliation snapshot, and future GitHub state create too many handoffs for a single-developer capstone.\",\n    \"Large generated reconciliation history is stored in the source repository even though only the approved current contract delta is needed for day-to-day development.\",\n    \"Milestone plans include artifact generation, supervisor, continuous autonomy, and parallelism before a single corrected delivery path exists.\"\n  ],\n  \"state_and_authority_concerns\": [\n    \"Necessary authorities are: approved GDD/design decisions for intent; task contract for bounded scope; integrated Git tree for implementation; deterministic/Unity/human validation for acceptance; and human merge/canon approval.\",\n    \"It is useful to distinguish a provider claim from test evidence and current conformance from dispatch permission, but those distinctions do not each require a heavyweight independent subsystem.\",\n    \"Reconciliation snapshots are valid audit history, but they duplicate responsibility when treated as a standing operational layer alongside Tasks and current conformance.\",\n    \"Task contracts should not retain mutable repository-state observations as if they remain current facts.\",\n    \"AgentRuntime versus TaskExecution is a reasonable generic/task-specific boundary, but it currently adds audit ceremony without an execution consumer.\",\n    \"Operational run state should live in one restartable supervisor record or PR/check state, not be recreated across task files, evidence records, runtime artifacts, future GitHub fields, and status documents.\",\n    \"Git commit/PR identity plus a compact validation manifest can replace much of the bespoke evidence DAG for ordinary tasks; richer lineage is warranted only for revalidation or regulated/high-risk surfaces.\",\n    \"Human authority is currently correctly retained, but fail-closed authorization has become a permanent stop rather than a guard around an enabled narrow path.\"\n  ],\n  \"strong_decisions\": [\n    \"A deterministic local process—not an LLM context—should own continuity, budgets, retries, and recovery.\",\n    \"Workers should receive one bounded task and should not reconstruct the global roadmap.\",\n    \"Git and Unity evidence must outrank worker claims.\",\n    \"Implementation should be isolated from main, and merged/integrated state should define delivery.\",\n    \"Runtime, visual, and interaction evidence must be able to overturn static approval.\",\n    \"Canonical Unity scenes and prefabs must not be mutated by normal tests.\",\n    \"Missing design should be escalated rather than silently invented.\",\n    \"No-op repairs must consume retry budget.\",\n    \"Start with one worker; add parallelism only after reliable delivery.\",\n    \"Reconciliation should propose reviewed changes rather than directly rewriting operational state.\",\n    \"Design completeness and execution size are legitimately different questions.\",\n    \"Provider-neutral generic invocation is useful when kept below game-specific task semantics.\"\n  ],\n  \"structural_flaws\": [\n    \"The implemented architecture ends before the activities that produce game value: selecting, authorizing, writing, validating in Unity, merging, and unlocking dependent work.\",\n    \"Schema-v2 removed task completion status and deliberately disabled readiness before evidence-based dependency readiness was implemented.\",\n    \"The moving-GDD model is global and hash-based rather than scoped and causal.\",\n    \"The bootstrap classified NSC-003 as concrete/single-agent even though the repository's own current-state document now requires multiple human design decisions before implementation.\",\n    \"Conformance verifies record consistency and selected surfaces, not the semantic truth of every repository observation copied into a contract or GDD.\",\n    \"Documentation is not a reliable current-state control plane because the same file contains incompatible next-step and implementation claims.\",\n    \"The architecture plans a generic scanner, context builder, decomposer, artifact authority, supervisor, and execution crew as separate milestones instead of proving the smallest vertical delivery path.\",\n    \"The provider boundary assumes externally enforced read-only containment for repository review; no equivalent approved containment/write policy exists for gameplay implementation.\",\n    \"The current canonical scene is still a generated monolithic integration surface, so many nominally independent tasks will contend on the builder and scene until prefab/runtime composition boundaries improve.\",\n    \"The project has optimized correctness metadata while the required game remains at door/mana/camera prototype maturity with no spells, enemies, navigation foundation, restart, victory, or build scene registration.\"\n  ],\n  \"throughput_assessment\": \"Major near-term leverage is not currently plausible. The simpler historical crews did produce a door prototype, mana system, and camera feature, showing that bounded AI implementation can help. The production rewrite has not reproduced that result. Since the camera feature, the frozen ancestry contains 244 commits, 136 touching Pipeline, three touching the game area, and zero touching runtime gameplay scripts. Today the machinery can validate its graph, retrieve canon, inspect one conformance baseline, and run bounded read-only reviews; it cannot advance a gameplay task. If forbidden to build infrastructure for one slice, the first failure is immediate: taskcontrol cannot select work, authorization is denied, and AgentRuntime cannot write or run Unity. Progress would require manually bypassing the production machinery and using a human-driven coding/Unity workflow.\",\n  \"verdict_reason\": \"The architecture's governing principles are sound and worth retaining, but its production partitioning, milestone order, and GDD synchronization model are not. Safety infrastructure has displaced game development, the operational graph was made inert, and evolving canon is handled with coarse invalidation rather than reviewed impact. Reorganize around one thin write-test-review-merge gameplay lane; only add infrastructure when that lane exposes a repeated bottleneck.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq '.result' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/llm_reliability_engineer.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq '.result' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/llm_reliability_engineer.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"alternative_architecture\": {\n    \"description\": \"Use a thin feature-delivery kernel. State: separate stable product requirements from engineering policy and generated repository inventory; bind feature contracts only to relevant requirement IDs. Planning: select and clarify one near-term vertical slice, with scoped impact analysis for later canon changes instead of global reconciliation. Execution: one write-capable agent in an isolated branch/worktree, using externally enforced file and command permissions. Validation: Git/scope checks, clean Unity Edit/Play Mode tests, one fresh semantic diff review, then targeted human experiential review. Recovery: preserve the branch and attempt journal, feed specific failure evidence into at most two repairs, then escalate. Unity integration: explicitly distinguish in-memory builders from committed scenes/prefabs and require non-mutating validation. Add deterministic scheduling only after several successful deliveries.\",\n    \"needed\": true,\n    \"why_better\": \"It preserves the strongest current safety boundaries while removing global verifier swarms, duplicated state, prompt anchoring, and provider infrastructure from the gameplay critical path.\"\n  },\n  \"architecture_summary\": \"The architecture contains sound safety primitives but is not sound enough, as currently organized and implemented, for autonomous Unity delivery. It is assurance-heavy and delivery-light: canon retrieval, graph validation, evidence modeling, reconciliation, and provider transport exist, but no production path can write a gameplay change, invoke Unity, perform GER, derive readiness, dispatch, or merge. Its moving-canon model is especially weak because product design, engineering policy, and dated repository facts are mixed together and synchronized through duplicated artifacts.\",\n  \"biggest_uncertainty\": \"Actual model spend is not normalized or retained comparably. Cost severity is inferred from prompt sizes, worker counts, turn limits, retries, and history rather than invoices. Feature throughput has also never been measured through a complete production delivery.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"do_not_build_yet\": [\n    \"Continuous supervisor or autonomous scheduler\",\n    \"Parallel workers and worktree pools\",\n    \"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization\",\n    \"Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority platform\",\n    \"More provider migrations or cross-provider comparison infrastructure\",\n    \"Another full-project reconciliation run\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"At the frozen clean HEAD, taskcontrol validates 37 contracts, but readiness is explicitly unavailable and zero tasks are authorized for dispatch.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The authoritative scene moved to Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity in commit 484e66a, but 16 task contracts, RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, and GDD canon still reference the deleted nested scene. Structural task validation nevertheless passes.\",\n      \"path\": \"Tasks/; Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml; Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml; Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Current conformance hashes the entire GDD and marks evidence stale when that hash changes, regardless of whether the edit affects the task.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py:164\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The production reconciliation prompt suite totals 4,251 lines and contains dated closure sections prescribing conclusions repaired during earlier rounds.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/Reconciliation/prompts/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Nine reconciliation workers receive prior routing hints and the same complete key registry. Verifier diversity defaults to Claude opus and sonnet aliases, preserving provider-family and prompt correlation.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/Reconciliation/parallel_reconciliation_agent.py:617; Pipeline/Reconciliation/verification_crew.py:71\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Parallel verification defines nine domain coverage audits plus six evidence/structure/execution audits before refiners and selective re-verification.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/Reconciliation/parallel_verification_crew.py:196\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Production pipeline Python totals approximately 24,623 lines, compared with approximately 1,508 lines of Unity C# game code.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/; Assets/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"History contains 56 commits touching Reconciliation, 41 touching TaskGraph, and 21 touching AgentRuntime/TaskExecution/ArchitectureReview, versus 7 commits touching Assets.\",\n      \"path\": \"Git history through 9f2485dca1b61360e6d02810adc71e021346496e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Assignment 6 records two static evaluator passes followed by two human Unity runtime failures, then a refiner claim that made no Assets changes.\",\n      \"path\": \"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md:90\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"CURRENT_STATE first says the Codex ArchitectureReview migration is implemented, then later says Claude migration is next and Codex remains unimplemented.\",\n      \"path\": \"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:48; Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:631\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Read-only checks executed successfully: taskcontrol validate, taskcontrol ready, NSC-023 state, and GDDRAG validate. HEAD/tree and the worktree remained unchanged; NSC-023 is the sole demonstrated conformant production task.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gdd_iteration_concerns\": [\n    \"The root GDD mixes gameplay intent, agent workflow policy, package choices, build configuration, and dated repository inventory. An engineering change can therefore appear to be a game-design change.\",\n    \"Whole-document hashing creates global revalidation pressure from unrelated canon edits.\",\n    \"Sequential RAG chunk IDs are reproducible but are not durable requirement identities across heading insertion or reordering.\",\n    \"Task contracts copy GDD prose and bootstrap repository observations, creating stale replicas instead of durable references.\",\n    \"No demonstrated workflow maps a changed clause to only the affected contracts, code/assets, tests, and evidence.\",\n    \"The scene relocation proves synchronization is not transactional: production code, tests, and evidence moved while canon, resource claims, and task evidence did not.\",\n    \"Routine GDD evolution needs a reviewed requirement-level impact workflow. Full reconciliation should be an exceptional audit, not the normal synchronization mechanism.\"\n  ],\n  \"human_intervention_points\": [\n    \"Approve ambiguous gameplay mechanics and input arbitration. NSC-003 currently lacks enough decisions for a safe handoff.\",\n    \"Approve genuine canon or architecture changes rather than letting an agent infer design.\",\n    \"Perform Play Mode, input-feel, framing, readability, animation, visual-quality, and balance judgments.\",\n    \"Inspect scene, prefab, package, and build-setting changes where serialization or editor behavior matters.\",\n    \"Review and merge initially; merge automation should wait for repeated delivery evidence.\",\n    \"Decide whether a circuit-breaker failure requires repair, task rescoping, contract change, or design change.\"\n  ],\n  \"hypothetical_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"AgentRuntime exact-type, polymorphic-container, Windows device-name, deep-JSON, and immutable-publication hardening protects mostly adversarial transport cases not experienced during game delivery.\",\n    \"Evidence-record cycle, incomparable-ancestry, and ambiguity logic is covered synthetically but has no real production revalidation history.\",\n    \"GitHub mirroring, leases, merge queues, and parallel resource scheduling address future scale, not the current single-worker bottleneck.\",\n    \"Artifact Authority and style GER address future generated design/content; the current graph has zero artifact tasks.\",\n    \"Eight-role ArchitectureReview provider provenance and future cross-provider comparison do not advance gameplay delivery.\",\n    \"Automatic backlog replenishment and continuous supervision protect a future autonomous queue that does not yet exist.\"\n  ],\n  \"missing_components\": [\n    \"A production end-to-end gameplay lane from approved contract through implementation, Unity validation, review, merge, and evidence.\",\n    \"Stable requirement/clause identities and scoped GDD-change impact links.\",\n    \"A write-capable worker boundary and externally enforced approved command execution.\",\n    \"Production ExecutionCrew/GER integration, or a substantially thinner equivalent.\",\n    \"Restartable attempt/lease state for one real task.\",\n    \"Cross-representation referential validation covering canon-described paths, task resource claims, builders, tests, and actual Unity assets.\",\n    \"Automated compact delivery/revalidation receipt creation.\",\n    \"Per-feature token, latency, retry, defect, and human-minute telemetry.\",\n    \"A real production revalidation example; only NSC-023 has a baseline.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_slice\": {\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"Obtain a one-page human-approved input decision covering click/hold semantics, UI/gameplay arbitration, destination replacement and cancellation, arrival tolerance, and pathing expectations.\",\n      \"Supersede or split NSC-003. Make the first contract cover shared pointer projection plus visible click-to-destination/hold-steer movement; defer restriction/reset/suspend APIs unless required by the implementation seam.\",\n      \"Correct the authoritative scene path across GDD engineering facts, task/resource claims, and project requirements, then add one deterministic cross-representation path check.\",\n      \"Implement the movement slice in one isolated branch using Input Actions, shared gameplay-plane projection, scene-builder wiring, and the committed Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity artifact.\",\n      \"Run clean targeted Edit/Play Mode validation, obtain human movement-feel approval, perform one fresh semantic diff review, merge, and publish one compact delivery receipt.\"\n    ],\n    \"proof_of_value\": \"Within one working day, an approved brief becomes merged, visibly playable mouse-directed movement with clean Unity evidence, bounded model usage, no global reconciliation, and no manual repair of duplicated operational state. Record elapsed time, model calls/tokens where available, repair count, escaped defects, and human minutes.\",\n    \"title\": \"NSC-003A mouse movement vertical slice through a thin delivery lane\",\n    \"why\": \"It is player-visible, unlocks Fireball, Frost Field, and door targeting, and tests the actual value proposition more directly than another infrastructure milestone.\"\n  },\n  \"observed_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"Runtime evidence re-entering GER directly addresses the camera’s two static-pass/runtime-fail incidents.\",\n    \"No-op detection and circuit breakers address the observed refiner claim that made no Assets change. Progress should, however, be tied to resolving a named failure rather than merely producing any diff.\",\n    \"The non-saving in-memory scene-builder seam and clean Unity runner address observed canonical-scene mutation risk from builder tests.\",\n    \"Production GDDRAG freshness and integrity replace the actually stale July Assignment 4 knowledge base.\",\n    \"Scene centralization and meta-identity checks address the earlier duplicate authoritative-scene ambiguity.\",\n    \"Raw-output preservation, bounded retries, finding identities, and deterministic validators address observed reconciliation parsing, max-turn, dangling-edge, attribution, and refinement failures.\",\n    \"Separating task contracts from mutable completion status closes a discovered authority vulnerability, although no bad autonomous dispatch actually occurred.\"\n  ],\n  \"overall_verdict\": \"partially_unsound\",\n  \"overengineering\": [\n    \"Approximately 24.6k lines of pipeline Python precede a single write-capable gameplay execution lane.\",\n    \"A 37-task graph was produced through nine generation workers and up to fifteen parallel auditors, with refiners and selective pass two layered afterward.\",\n    \"The 4,251-line reconciliation prompt suite accumulates specific closure patches, raising maintenance cost and anchoring future reviewers.\",\n    \"AgentRuntime heavily hardens hostile JSON and path cases in a trusted single-user environment while repository writing and approved command execution remain unsupported.\",\n    \"ArchitectureReview provider migration proves transport reuse, not game-development throughput.\",\n    \"WORK_ID_MAP and persisted resource-group membership duplicate relationships derivable from task contracts.\",\n    \"CURRENT_STATE, START_HERE, master context, milestone documents, ADR summaries, and reconciliation current views duplicate present-tense state and have already diverged.\"\n  ],\n  \"state_and_authority_concerns\": [\n    \"Necessary authorities are: human-approved product canon; bounded feature/task contracts; integrated Git state; isolated attempt state; deterministic test/runtime evidence; human experiential approval; and derived readiness/merge state.\",\n    \"The current separation of task definition from completion evidence is sound. Model/provider claims also correctly lack test, merge, or conformance authority.\",\n    \"Dated repository inventory and pipeline architecture should not live in root game-design canon. Put them in generated repository facts and engineering policy.\",\n    \"Reconciliation snapshots are useful audit history, but Tasks, WORK_ID_MAP, RESOURCE_GROUPS, PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS, copied GDD prose, current-state documents, and mutable reconciliation views duplicate responsibility.\",\n    \"Conformance is simultaneously under-sensitive and over-sensitive: manually chosen surfaces may omit causal dependencies, while a whole-GDD hash invalidates unrelated tasks.\",\n    \"Resource-group files duplicate task claims and validate internal agreement rather than whether the referenced Unity resource still exists.\",\n    \"GitHub may become a dashboard, but it must not become a second operational authority without a single explicit owner.\",\n    \"The GDD assigns humans architecture, merging, scene inspection, playtesting, balance, and final integration. The resulting system is assisted development, not high autonomy, until some of those steps are safely narrowed or automated.\"\n  ],\n  \"strong_decisions\": [\n    \"Deterministic tools own graph computation, Git identity, schema checks, test execution facts, and clean-tree checks.\",\n    \"Workers and providers cannot self-declare delivery, conformance, readiness, or authorization.\",\n    \"Runtime and Unity evidence can override a semantic/static pass.\",\n    \"Task definitions are separated from current completion truth.\",\n    \"Branches/worktrees should precede parallelism, and Unity shared-asset locking should be conservative.\",\n    \"RAG is correctly treated as canon retrieval rather than repository truth.\",\n    \"Progressive decomposition and explicit human authority for missing design are sensible principles.\",\n    \"Starting with one worker and bounding retries is appropriate.\",\n    \"The testing policy correctly distinguishes builder capability from committed-artifact conformance.\"\n  ],\n  \"structural_flaws\": [\n    \"Evolving design is framed mainly as snapshot reconciliation and invalidation instead of routine scoped change management.\",\n    \"Verification independence is overstated because workers share canon, candidate framing, prior routing keys, the key registry, provider family, and prescriptive closure prompts.\",\n    \"Unioning every verifier finding reduces false-negative risk but amplifies false-positive cost and destabilizes reconciliation.\",\n    \"The production critical path is missing: no write-capable task execution, orchestrated Unity run, production GER, readiness, dispatch, or merge.\",\n    \"Deterministic checks are strongest at artifact shape and transport boundaries but miss cross-representation referential integrity, as the deleted scene path demonstrates.\",\n    \"The no-op rule can incentivize irrelevant churn. Assignment 6’s final pass added null-target hardening while the substantive framing repair had already occurred elsewhere.\",\n    \"The milestone sequence optimized architecture assurance before feature throughput and has become self-reinforcing.\",\n    \"Provider-neutrality is implemented below an absent product workflow; abstraction arrived before the first production consumer that matters.\"\n  ],\n  \"throughput_assessment\": \"Current near-term leverage is low. The system can retrieve canon, validate graph shape, inspect one camera baseline, and harden model transport, but it cannot autonomously advance gameplay. Dispatch is disabled, workers cannot write or run approved commands, Unity/GER is not integrated, and only one task has production evidence. The machinery may improve assurance after attachment to a delivery lane, but it is not currently credible for turning weeks into days. A thin single-feature lane could plausibly create major leverage quickly; the planned supervisor, decomposer, GitHub, and parallel-worker milestones would not.\",\n  \"verdict_reason\": \"The core philosophy is sound, but the current architecture is partially unsound because its moving-canon and state-synchronization model has already drifted, semantic verification is correlated and prompt-anchored, and most investment lies outside the gameplay-delivery critical path. Preserve deterministic evidence, runtime validation, isolation, bounded retries, and human design authority. Reorganize around one real feature at a time and freeze or remove infrastructure that does not measurably reduce delivery time or escaped defects.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq '.result' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/unity_production_engineer.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"jq '.result' Pipeline/ArchitectureReview/outputs/codex/runs/20260823T102213Z-35a76864/reviews/unity_production_engineer.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"alternative_architecture\": {\n    \"description\": \"Reorganize around a thin, single-feature delivery ledger. State: stable requirement IDs/revisions plus Git, small near-frontier contracts, append-only attempt journals, and delivery receipts. Planning: human selects one feature; a planner and Unity scanner validate one contract and its actual paths/GUIDs. Execution: one writable provider in an isolated worktree. Validation: deterministic diff/scope checks, Unity compile, EditMode/PlayMode tests, exact committed-scene inspection, semantic review, and human playtesting. Recovery: preserve branch commits and stage journals, resume from the failed stage, and circuit-break after bounded repairs. Unity integration: serialize only through approved editor/builder operations, retain `.meta` identity, run one host Unity job at a time, and compare canonical asset bytes before/after tests.\",\n    \"needed\": true,\n    \"why_better\": \"This preserves the good safety boundaries but removes global reconciliation, provider parity, artifact generation, GitHub synchronization, and parallel scheduling from the critical path. Requirement-level revisions prevent unrelated GDD edits from invalidating every delivered task, while a task preflight prevents stale Unity paths and GUIDs from entering execution. Most importantly, it produces gameplay evidence before investing further in platform machinery.\"\n  },\n  \"architecture_summary\": \"The core topology is good: bounded workers, Git as integrated truth, deterministic validation, runtime feedback, immutable evidence, and human design/merge authority. The current composition is partially unsound because it lacks an end-to-end writable Unity delivery lane and duplicates mutable project facts across too many stores. An ordinary human-approved scene relocation already left canon, 16 contracts, project requirements, and resource locks pointing at a deleted asset while structural validation still passed.\",\n  \"biggest_uncertainty\": \"No real gameplay task has passed through the current AgentRuntime/TaskExecution architecture. Actual implementation quality, Unity failure rate, repair cost, and end-to-end cycle time remain unmeasured; the camera evidence predates the production execution lane.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"do_not_build_yet\": [\n    \"Parallel workers, generalized worktree scheduling, or merge queues.\",\n    \"GitHub Issues/Projects synchronization.\",\n    \"Provider fallback or additional provider-comparison/review machinery.\",\n    \"A general Progressive Decomposer and Artifact Authority platform before a real task is blocked by missing design.\",\n    \"Style evaluation or automated artifact generation.\",\n    \"A broad incremental project scanner; add only the Unity/task preflight needed by the next slice.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The checked-out clean tree is exactly the required frozen commit 9f2485dca1b61360e6d02810adc71e021346496e.\",\n      \"path\": \"/workspace\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Read-only execution of `taskcontrol validate` passed structurally with 37 active contracts, but autonomous dispatch remained disabled. NSC-023 derived `conformant`; NSC-003 derived `not_delivered`. No Unity tests were executed during this review.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Production ExecutionCrew orchestration, Unity execution, task selection, readiness, dispatch, Git workflow, merging, and provider fallback are explicitly unimplemented.\",\n      \"path\": \"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Both live provider adapters reject repository writing and approved command execution, so AgentRuntime cannot implement a gameplay task.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/README.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"TaskExecution only binds a task identity to one invocation; it explicitly owns no selection, Git, Unity, GER, evidence publication, or completion transition.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskExecution/README.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Commit 484e66a moved the populated authoritative scene and its `.meta` identity to `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity`; commit 86af98f added path/GUID safeguards.\",\n      \"path\": \"Git history at 484e66a and 86af98f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Sixteen active task contracts still cite the deleted `Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` path.\",\n      \"path\": \"Tasks/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The GDD still declares the deleted nested scene canonical and the populated `Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity` non-canonical, despite the later human-approved relocation.\",\n      \"path\": \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Project requirements and the shared scene resource group retain the same obsolete path, so future lock acquisition would not protect the real scene.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.yaml and Pipeline/TaskGraph/RESOURCE_GROUPS.yaml\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The graph validator checks resource-key consistency but not whether `repo-file`, `unity-scene`, repository-evidence, or GUID targets exist.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/work_graph_validate.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The scene-location smoke test correctly protects uniqueness and GUID 92dbd0a3e6c18e245896a66c5120379d, but only scans active C# for obsolete references; it does not cover canon or task metadata.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/Testing/scene_location_smoke_test.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"NSC-023 is reported conformant even though its bound contract still contains stale scene repository evidence; its evidence record separately points at the current scene. The evaluator verifies hashes, gates, and listed surfaces, not factual consistency of repository-evidence prose.\",\n      \"path\": \"Tasks/NSC-023.yaml and Pipeline/TaskGraph/evidence/NSC-023/records/BASE-NSC-023-86af98f41ab5.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Conformance binds the normalized hash of the entire GDD. Any GDD edit stales existing evidence, while only a contract hash/revision change produces `needs_replan`. Conformance surfaces are manually enumerated.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"A passing camera EditMode suite previously invoked the saving production builder and rewrote the canonical tracked scene. The non-saving builder seam and clean runner were created in response.\",\n      \"path\": \"Pipeline/Testing/README.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"The camera twice passed static evaluation but failed human Unity testing for direction, following, and framing; a later refiner also claimed implementation while making no asset change.\",\n      \"path\": \"Assignment6GER/README_Assignment6.md and Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Since August 21, reachable history contains roughly 205 commits, only three of which touch Assets; those Asset changes concern test safety and scene centralization rather than a new gameplay feature. The repository has 303 pipeline/task/AI-document files versus 51 tracked Asset files.\",\n      \"path\": \"Git history through 9f2485d\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"NSC-003 is classified as `single_agent` despite spanning Input Actions, pointer projection, locomotion, restriction/reset/suspend interfaces, builder wiring, serialized-scene integration, and unresolved input arbitration. Current PlayerMovement still directly polls `Keyboard.current`.\",\n      \"path\": \"Tasks/NSC-003.yaml and Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerMovement.cs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"observation\": \"Unity 6000.1.8f1 is pinned and the Input System is installed, but Build Settings contain no scenes and the required Tilemap/AI Navigation packages are not configured yet.\",\n      \"path\": \"ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt, ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset, and Packages/manifest.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gdd_iteration_concerns\": [\n    \"The architecture currently treats the whole GDD as one versioned unit. An unrelated wording, balance, or room edit will require revalidation of every task whose evidence binds the previous document hash.\",\n    \"A semantic GDD change can require a new contract, different dependencies, implementation rollback, or cancellation. Returning only `needs_revalidation` against the old contract frames design evolution incorrectly.\",\n    \"There are no stable requirement IDs/revisions in canon and no implemented causal mapping from changed requirements to contracts, code/assets, tests, and downstream obligations.\",\n    \"Reconciliation is correctly immutable, but the reviewed graph-delta/apply process for later changes is not implemented. The scene relocation demonstrates that ordinary repository evolution can bypass synchronization.\",\n    \"Repository/process facts should not be copied into root design canon unless maintained transactionally. Canon currently contradicts Git about the authoritative scene.\",\n    \"The future change flow should classify edits as editorial, tuning, additive, changed, or removed; update only affected contracts; supersede contracts when meaning changes; and preserve unaffected delivery evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"human_intervention_points\": [\n    \"Choose actual product priority; graph order and apparent readiness are not sufficient.\",\n    \"Resolve NSC-003 input arbitration, click-versus-hold semantics, destination replacement/cancellation, arrival/pathing behavior, and restriction ownership before execution.\",\n    \"Approve normative GDD changes and reviewed contract additions, revisions, supersessions, or cancellations.\",\n    \"Inspect scene/prefab references, Inspector assignments, asset imports, and serialized diffs in the Unity Editor.\",\n    \"Run PlayMode checks for game feel, framing, pointer behavior, animation/readability, balance, and Console errors.\",\n    \"Perform Windows build inspection and approve package/build-setting changes.\",\n    \"Review and merge the task branch; automatic merge is not currently justified.\"\n  ],\n  \"hypothetical_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"Deep adversarial freezing of provider JSON subtypes and polymorphic containers protects a future hostile/malformed adapter boundary more than an experienced Unity delivery failure.\",\n    \"Cross-provider ArchitectureReview provenance, latest-pointer, and resume support improves review infrastructure but not gameplay throughput.\",\n    \"Provider fallback and cross-provider-equivalent budgeting are future operational concerns.\",\n    \"Parallel worktree claims, GitHub dashboards, merge queues, and continuous scheduling protect a later multi-worker system.\",\n    \"Artifact Authority, generated-design GER, and style evaluation protect future content-generation cases; the current graph contains no initial artifact task and no demonstrated blocking artifact flow.\"\n  ],\n  \"missing_components\": [\n    \"A small approved NSC-003 child contract with resolved input behavior.\",\n    \"A writable, bounded Implementer path using one provider and an isolated branch/worktree.\",\n    \"Task-scoped orchestration from contract to implementation result, deterministic diff, validation, repair, and escalation.\",\n    \"A host Unity execution bridge around the existing clean PowerShell runner.\",\n    \"Deterministic task preflight that validates referenced files, canonical scenes, `.meta` GUIDs, Input Action identities, packages, builder ownership, and Build Settings.\",\n    \"Automatic capture of actual changed paths and scope violations from Git rather than provider claims.\",\n    \"A reviewed evidence publisher that binds actual clean Unity XML, commit/tree, changed surfaces, human approval, and integrated commit.\",\n    \"Requirement-level GDD change-impact analysis and deterministic reviewed contract-delta application.\",\n    \"A derived readiness policy based on current conformance and dependency state; it should remain human-dispatched initially.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_slice\": {\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"Record a human-approved movement micro-brief resolving click/hold input arbitration, destination replacement/cancellation, arrival/pathing, and UI/spell/door click ownership.\",\n      \"Correct the authoritative scene path in canon, affected task/resource metadata, and validation so this drift cannot recur silently.\",\n      \"Supersede or split NSC-003 into a bounded first contract: Input Actions-based pointer projection plus click/hold player movement. Leave restriction/reset/suspend integration as a follow-up if it cannot remain independently testable.\",\n      \"Add only the minimal one-task writable runner needed to invoke one provider in an isolated worktree and capture the real Git diff.\",\n      \"Implement the movement slice in PlayerMovement, Input Actions, the builder, and the authoritative committed scene without regenerating `.meta` identity.\",\n      \"Add isolated component/PlayMode tests plus direct committed-scene conformance checks, run them through the clean Unity host runner, and complete a human feel/input check.\",\n      \"Merge through human review and publish one exact delivery record; use it to prove the first evidence-derived dependency/readiness transition.\"\n    ],\n    \"proof_of_value\": \"One approved gameplay contract travels from planned to implemented, cleanly Unity-tested, human-playtested, merged, evidence-published, and currently conformant at HEAD. Measure elapsed time, model invocations, repair count, human minutes, and escaped defects. That is the first credible evidence that the architecture makes development materially faster.\",\n    \"title\": \"NSC-003A — End-to-End Mouse Movement Delivery Lane\",\n    \"why\": \"This is the smallest slice that exercises the actual value chain and unlocks spells and door interaction. If infrastructure additions were forbidden, the first autonomous failure would be immediate: current providers cannot write or execute commands. With an ordinary human-driven coding agent, the first semantic failure would be NSC-003's unresolved input contract; after implementation, Unity execution and evidence publication would still be manual. This slice exposes and closes all three gaps without building the later platform.\"\n  },\n  \"observed_failure_solutions\": [\n    \"Runtime Unity feedback feeding GER solved camera direction, following, and framing defects missed by static semantic review.\",\n    \"The no-op progress guard prevented a refiner's unchanged `implemented` claim from being accepted and charged it against the repair budget.\",\n    \"The non-saving in-memory builder seam separated builder capability from canonical serialized state and stopped tests from saving the production scene.\",\n    \"Direct committed-scene tests, byte comparison, and the clean runner address the experienced destructive passing-test incident.\",\n    \"Moving the scene with its `.meta`, asserting one authoritative scene, and checking the GUID address the duplicate-scene/asset-identity incident.\",\n    \"Immutable reconciliation runs, recovery scripts, bounded retries, and deterministic finding identities address actual max-turn, timeout, interrupted-run, and ordering failures visible in history.\",\n    \"Schema-v2 contracts and committed conformance evidence prevent a mutable task status or worker claim from becoming completion truth, although autonomous dispatch had not yet experienced that failure in production.\",\n    \"Production GDDRAG fixes the demonstrated staleness of the older Assignment 4 index, while correctly not claiming top-k coverage completeness.\"\n  ],\n  \"overall_verdict\": \"partially_unsound\",\n  \"overengineering\": [\n    \"The project implemented two live provider adapters and migrated an eight-role architecture-review consumer before enabling one provider to write a gameplay change.\",\n    \"The accepted staged plan requires both adapters and full ExecutionCrew roles before the first real provider-interchangeable task proof; that ordering optimizes abstraction confidence ahead of product throughput.\",\n    \"Global multi-model reconciliation, verification, streaming refinement, recovery, migrations, and immutable histories consumed substantial effort for a 37-contract bootstrap. They should not become the normal response to iterative GDD edits.\",\n    \"There are multiple overlapping architecture/status documents with already-stale milestone claims. Operational status should be generated from code where possible.\",\n    \"The repository's recent commit/file ratio shows infrastructure becoming a second product: extensive pipeline churn has not produced a post-camera gameplay feature.\",\n    \"Provider trust-boundary hardening is technically strong, but much of its depth has lower current expected value than a writable task lane, Unity preflight, and one real gameplay delivery.\"\n  ],\n  \"state_and_authority_concerns\": [\n    \"Necessary boundaries: approved GDD/feature decisions define intent; task contracts define bounded work and gates; Git defines integrated code/assets; attempt journals define transient execution; evidence receipts plus current Git derive conformance; humans own ambiguous design, visual/feel approval, and merge authority.\",\n    \"Necessary separation: generic AgentRuntime must not own NSC task identity, and TaskExecution audit artifacts must not become completion evidence. The ADR-039 direction is correct.\",\n    \"Duplicated responsibility: authoritative scene paths and other repository facts appear in GDD prose, task repository evidence, exclusive-resource keys, project requirements, RAG chunks, current-state documents, and conformance surfaces.\",\n    \"The living graph is called operational state, but schema v2 intentionally contains no operational status and readiness is disabled. It is currently a contract/dependency catalog, not an operational work graph.\",\n    \"Manual conformance-surface selection can under-approximate Unity dependencies. A package, Input Action, prefab, ProjectSetting, referenced ScriptableObject, or builder dependency omitted from the receipt can change without invalidating conformance.\",\n    \"Reconciliation history should remain audit history, but it should not be a prerequisite authority layer for routine local changes. A requirement/task delta plus human approval is enough.\",\n    \"GitHub should remain a projection/dashboard if introduced; it must not duplicate contract, evidence, or conformance authority.\"\n  ],\n  \"strong_decisions\": [\n    \"One bounded worker and human merge authority before parallelism are appropriate for Unity's shared serialized assets.\",\n    \"Workers and provider adapters produce claims, never test, merge, readiness, or completion truth.\",\n    \"Task contracts are separated from mutable completion status, and committed Git objects—not a dirty working copy—drive conformance evaluation.\",\n    \"Exact commit/tree, artifact blob, task revision, canon hash, and human approval binding make evidence auditable.\",\n    \"Unity tests must start and finish with a clean tree, parse XML, preserve logs, and report exact Unity version and limitations.\",\n    \"Builder output and committed serialized artifact conformance are treated as separate claims.\",\n    \"Scenes and prefabs move with `.meta` files; duplicate authoritative scenes are prohibited.\",\n    \"Runtime and visual evidence can override a static evaluator pass and return structured feedback to bounded repair.\",\n    \"Missing design is escalated rather than silently invented.\",\n    \"Parallelism, automatic merge, and autonomous dispatch remain disabled until a one-ticket lane is trustworthy.\"\n  ],\n  \"structural_flaws\": [\n    \"There is no end-to-end state machine connecting approved plan → writable execution → Git-observed changes → Unity validation → repair → human review → merge → delivery evidence → dependency readiness.\",\n    \"Moving canon is modeled as whole-document invalidation, not requirement-level versioning and impact. This will generate broad revalidation work while still failing to revise contracts whose meaning changed.\",\n    \"Unity asset authority is duplicated and already contradictory after one routine human-approved relocation. Structural validation passes because it verifies key consistency rather than target existence and GUID identity.\",\n    \"The current graph can label an item `single_agent` without resolving gameplay choices or proving its Unity integration surface is bounded; NSC-003 is the concrete counterexample.\",\n    \"A conformance record can be current while descriptive repository evidence inside its bound contract is factually stale, because only hashes, declared gates, and manually selected surfaces are evaluated.\",\n    \"The production runtime deliberately cannot write or execute approved commands, and the Unity runner remains an external manual operation. Therefore the current architecture is an audit/review platform, not an autonomous development pipeline.\",\n    \"The milestone ordering puts compact context, decomposition, provider parity, and generalized crew infrastructure ahead of the shortest working gameplay loop, despite the stated real-slice rule.\",\n    \"Worktree isolation alone does not solve Unity production integration. Each candidate still needs a viable Unity project/library strategy, serialized asset inspection, exclusive host execution, and post-rebase validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"throughput_assessment\": \"Major near-term leverage is not yet demonstrated. The architecture has materially improved safety, repeatability, and auditability, especially around Unity tests and camera validation. But at the frozen commit, zero tasks are dispatchable, providers cannot edit, NSC-003 is not safely specified, Unity validation is external, and evidence publication is manual. Recent history is overwhelmingly pipeline work with no new gameplay feature. The system is therefore slower than direct expert-assisted development today; it becomes plausibly high-leverage only after the proposed vertical slice proves a repeatable one-ticket cycle.\",\n  \"verdict_reason\": \"The foundational production instincts are strong, so this is not a fundamentally wrong approach. It is partially unsound because moving-design synchronization, Unity asset authority, and the execution-to-evidence path are either incorrectly framed or absent. The existing stale-scene contradiction is direct evidence that the current stores do not stay coherent, and the lack of a writable Unity delivery lane means the architecture cannot yet achieve its stated days-instead-of-weeks goal.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
