{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"architecture_classification\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"change_or_replace\":[],\"critical_risks\":[],\"decision_rationale\":\"All eight reviews converge on the same high-level diagnosis, so repetition is not being treated as proof. The decisive evidence to verify is: whether the architecture actually lacks a delivery transaction; whether whole-GDD hashing causes both over- and under-invalidation; whether scene authority is genuinely split; and whether the proposed first slice should favor low ambiguity (mana) or higher dependency leverage (movement).\",\"defer_or_delete\":[],\"evidence_gaps\":[\"No current production gameplay task is claimed to have traversed write, Unity validation, repair, merge, and evidence publication; this must be confirmed from primary implementation/docs.\",\"The two candidate first slices make different claims about value: NSC-005 minimizes design and integration risk; NSC-003A exercises more architecture but requires human decisions.\"],\"executive_verdict\":\"Primary-evidence cross-check in progress.\",\"expected_autonomy_and_throughput\":\"Not yet finalized.\",\"gdd_iteration_strategy\":\"Not yet finalized.\",\"major_disagreements\":[{\"assessment\":\"Unresolved pending primary contract and runtime inspection.\",\"issue\":\"First implementation slice\",\"positions\":[\"NSC-005 mana reset and denied-spend feedback: shortest, least ambiguous delivery proof.\",\"NSC-003A mouse movement: higher player/dependency value and broader end-to-end stress test.\"]}],\"minimum_viable_architecture\":\"Not yet finalized.\",\"preserve\":[],\"recommended_next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[],\"success_test\":\"Will require an executed clean-tree Unity run plus explicit human runtime acceptance, not source inspection alone.\",\"title\":\"Between NSC-005 and a split NSC-003A\",\"why\":\"Primary evidence will decide.\"}}"}}
