{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"wc -l Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md\nrg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"354 Docs/AI-Pipeline/06_PROVIDER_NEUTRAL_EXECUTION_CREW_PLAN.md\n1:# Provider-Neutral Execution Crew Plan\r\n3:## Purpose\r\n11:## Existing reusable strengths\r\n34:## Provider-neutral rule\r\n42:## Proposed production structure\r\n83:## Provider-neutral contracts\r\n85:### Generic `AgentInvocationRequest`\n104:### Conceptual `AgentResult`\r\n122:## Provider adapters\r\n146:## Production roles\r\n150:### Implementer\r\n154:### Unity Test Author\r\n166:### Validator\r\n170:### Planning-role change\r\n176:## Model selection\r\n193:## Deterministic authority boundary\r\n212:## Run artifacts\r\n233:## Relationship to GER\r\n247:## Relationship to TaskGraph\r\n261:## Historical compatibility\r\n270:## Staged implementation plan\r\n274:### Stage 0 - Documentation and architecture approval\r\n281:### Stage 1 - Canonical Unity testing policy and deterministic clean runner\r\n288:### Stage 2 - Complete NSC-023 Phase 3 baseline/revalidation proof\r\n295:### Stage 3 - Extract provider-neutral `AgentRuntime`\r\n302:### Stage 4 - Implement Claude and OpenAI adapters against the same fixtures\r\n309:### Stage 5 - Create provider-neutral ExecutionCrew roles\r\n316:### Stage 6 - Prove one task with a mixed or interchangeable provider configuration\r\n323:### Stage 7 - Connect execution outputs to GER and Phase 3 evidence\r\n330:### Stage 8 - Consider readiness/dispatch only after repeated successful real deliveries\r\n337:## Branch strategy\r\n345:## Immediate next slice\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
